Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Found the solution. Apparently these up/down arrows are called "spinners" (sounds like something from the 1980s) and part of WebKit desktop browsers. Below is code to get rid of them and discussion on stackoverflow <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3975769/disable-webkits-spin-buttons-on-input-type-number>.

input[type=number]::-webkit-inner-spin-button,
input[type=number]::-webkit-outer-spin-button {
    -webkit-appearance: none;
    margin: 0;
}

