I am trying to make a page that has a navbar with two tabs, one of which contains a tabset. But I can't get the tables to render when I use both tabs. Below is a minimal example. Am I missing something, perhaps related to these "id" and "value" variables being passed around?

library(shiny)

ui <- navbarPage(
  title='Navbar with Tabset',
  position='fixed-top',
  header=tags$style(type="text/css", "body {padding-top: 70px;}"),
  tabPanel(title='Tab1',
    tabsetPanel(
      tabPanel('Iris',dataTableOutput('iris')),
      tabPanel('Mtcars',dataTableOutput('mtcars')),
      position='left'
    )
  )
  # comment the 4 lines below and the first tab will work
  ,
  tabPanel('Tab2',
    dataTableOutput('iris')
  )
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {

  output$iris <- renderDataTable(iris)
  output$mtcars <- renderDataTable(mtcars)

}

shinyApp(server = server, ui = ui)

